Retroid Pocket's mainline kernel work, applied first on top of Linux 7.3.

Source: github.com/RetroidPocket/linux, branch retroidpocket/v7.3 at
2209a42da1a891d0d140293f5831c50e4aa9cc61 (71 commits on the v7.3 tag,
c03c1a14507d). patches/ is `git format-patch v7.3..2209a42`, unmodified; each
"From <sha>" line is the upstream commit.

What it brings: RP6/Nova/Duo panels, the HTR3212 LED driver with
suspend/resume, Eliza (Snapdragon 7 Gen 4, Retroid Pocket Duo) GPU/video/
camera clocks, GPU/CDSP/Iris DT nodes, WCN7750 Wi-Fi + Bluetooth, the Eliza
sound card, the soundwire highest-port and lpass-tx-macro SWR_MIC10/11 fixes
(were our 0570/0571), the PCIe iommu-cells fix (was our 0514), and the DPU
command-mode MERGE_3D / mixer split fixes.

skip lists the ones build.sh leaves out and why. Order: these, then
ROCKNIX's patches, then ours (see build.sh). With them in, ROCKNIX 0033
(HTR3212) and our 0514, 0535, 0570 are gone (same code or superseded).

Audio for the Retroid DTS (phase 2, not used yet): Retroid ships its own
topology (RetroidPocket/audioreach-topology, retroidpocket/v1.0.5) and UCM
(RetroidPocket/alsa-ucm-conf, retroidpocket/v1.2.16).
